    <!--Sourdough Bread-->
    <div class="dessert-card">
      
      <h2>Sourdough Bread</h2>
      <h4> A community favorite, boasting a crusty exterior and a soft, airy interior, embodying the classic sourdough charm</h4>
    <img src="Sourdough.png" alt="sourdough loaf" />
    <!-- Sourdough Bread - chatGPT - CCO 1.0-->
    <h3>Ingredients </h3>
    <li>1 cup sourdough starter</li>
    <li> 1 1/2 cups warm water</li>
    <li>4 cups bread flour</li>
    <li>1 1/2 teaspoons salt</li>
    
    <h3>Instructions</h3>

    <ol>
    <li> First mix the starter water and 3 cups of flour in a large bowl.That should create a sticky dough</li><br>      <li>Next, add salt and remaining flour 1 tablespoon at a time until they are fully incorporated </li>
      
      <img src="Sourdough2.png" alt="sourdough kneeding" />
      <!-- Sourdough Bread - chatGPT - CCO 1.0 -->
    <li>Then, kneed the dough on a floured surface for about 15 minutes </li><br>
      
    <li> Once the kneeding is done, place the dough in a lighty greased bowl, cover it, and let it rise for about 5 hours</li><br>
    <li>Finally, shape the dough into a loaf, and let it rest for 30 minutes </li><br>
    <li>When you are ready to bake, preheat your oven to 450 degrees F and bake for about 30 minutes until its golden brown</li><br>
     
    </ol>
